WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:05.050
After a long, tense wait, the final season
of Game of Thrones finally premiered on April

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:10.100
14, 2019, with the first episode coming in
at just under an hour — despite being packed

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.519
full of revelations, reunions, and more.

00:00:12.519 --> 00:00:16.810
The return of Jon Snow, Daenerys Targaryen,
the three living Lannisters, and a metric

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:20.780
ton more of the show's characters brought
a few answers and even more questions with

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:21.280
them.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:25.320
Questions like...did you catch when Mac from
It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia showed up?

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:31.140
Here's everything else of importance that
happened in the Game of Thrones season premiere

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:34.840
— and everything we still want to know for
the remaining episodes of the series.

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:40.640
The trailers leading up to the premiere offered
plenty of shots of Daenerys arriving at Winterfell,

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:44.660
and audiences didn't have to wait long — in
the very first shot of the season premiere,

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:49.309
a Winterfell boy climbs a tree to see Daenerys'
army arrive, with the Mother of Dragons and

00:00:49.309 --> 00:00:53.969
her right-hand man, Jon Snow, flanked by dragons,
Unsullied, and Dothraki as they arrive at

00:00:53.969 --> 00:00:55.240
the stronghold of the North.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:59.500
Appropriately for the chilly North, the welcome
is less than warm, considering Northerners

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:03.850
are instinctively distrustful of any foreigners,
especially a new Queen from the far South

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:05.610
with two enormous dragons.

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:08.140
It isn't just the townspeople who don't trust
Daenerys.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:12.330
Sansa, Jon's sister, immediately dislikes
the Dragon Queen, who she considers at once

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:15.920
naive and arrogant for trusting Cersei to
serve as an ally to the North.

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:20.420
Whatever Sansa's attitude might be, it's clear
that Daenerys' assimilation into the Northern

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:24.420
way of life won't be simple, and will likely
be a struggle for the rest of the season.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:29.490
Cersei Lannister is always one of the toughest
characters to read, and in the premiere, she's

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:31.220
just as inscrutable as ever.

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:35.860
Still astride the Iron Throne, she seems completely
unperturbed by news that the White Walkers

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:40.430
have breached the Wall, especially considering
that the Golden Company, an army of mercenaries

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:45.020
under Cersei's control, has just arrived at
King's Landing thanks to her unlikely fiancé,

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:46.160
Euron Greyjoy.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:50.420
After he delivers her new army, the two finally
consummate their relationship, which leads

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:54.360
to probably one of the least sexy post-romance
lines you'll hear all week:

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:57.700
"I'm going to put a prince in that belly."

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:07.740
As you might expect, the icy queen looks pretty
uncomfortable, sipping a glass of wine as

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:08.540
he leaves the room.

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:13.260
Last season, audiences heard Cersei tell Jamie
she was pregnant with Jaime's baby.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.060
"Who will you say is the father?"

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:16.060
"You."

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:23.900
Meanwhile, Tyrion found out about his new
niece or nephew a couple episodes later.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.499
That unborn child still seems to be a secret.

00:02:26.499 --> 00:02:31.060
So after she drove Jamie to abandon her at
the end of season 7, Cersei may manipulate

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:35.420
Euron into being the next man to unwittingly
claim one of Jaime and Cersei's kids as his

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:35.920
own.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:40.319
Whether Cersei is creeped out by her new boyfriend
— or if she's planning to pull a Maury and

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:43.820
tell Euron he's the father — we'll just
have to wait for a future episode to find

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:44.320
out.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:50.319
The most brutal reveal regarding Cersei ultimately
comes from Qyburn, her resident mad scientist,

00:02:50.319 --> 00:02:54.650
who shows up during one of Bronn's routine
brothel visits to casually tell him that Cersei

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:58.310
would like both of her brothers dead, and
the one to do it would be rewarded beyond

00:02:58.310 --> 00:02:59.599
his wildest dreams.

00:02:59.599 --> 00:03:03.610
Cersei obviously has a plan in place, but
how it will unfold is still anyone's guess.

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:08.579
Ever since viewers found out the truth about
Jon's parents — that he was actually born

00:03:08.579 --> 00:03:13.340
to a legally married Lyanna Stark and Rhaegar
Targaryen, making him an undisputed prince

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:17.360
— fans have been waiting for Jon to find
out too, and this episode got right to the

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:17.860
point.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:22.239
Aside from plenty of pointed comments about
who Jon "is," there's one huge moment in this

00:03:22.239 --> 00:03:26.959
episode hinting at Jon's true heritage, followed
by the big reveal that finally puts one of

00:03:26.959 --> 00:03:30.700
the show's biggest revelations in front of
the person it'll affect the most.

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:34.060
Jon, still blissfully ignorant to the fact
that he's been sleeping with his aunt —

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:40.860
— is having a lovely day-date with his new
girlfriend until she suggests that they ride

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.080
her two remaining dragons.

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:46.660
With Daenerys riding Drogon, the dragon she
always takes into battle, Jon is left with

00:03:46.669 --> 00:03:50.599
Rhaegal, who is actually named for his father,
Daenerys' brother Rhaegar.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:55.159
In the moment, it feels especially significant
that Rhaegal allows Jon to mount without protest.

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:59.160
However, at the end of the episode, the show
does away with all pretense that it will keep

00:03:59.169 --> 00:04:03.689
this secret, letting Sam tell Jon the entire
truth about who he is, much to Jon's shock

00:04:03.689 --> 00:04:07.920
— and naturally, it all happens right in
front of Ned Stark's statue in the crypt.

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:13.320
Reunions between favorite characters rank
among the most important and anticipated moments

00:04:13.329 --> 00:04:16.940
in this season, and the premiere certainly
didn't disappoint — even though some of

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:18.430
them weren't particularly happy.

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:22.360
Arya and Jon's reunion at the Godswood in
Winterfell was certainly one of the episode's

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:26.210
most emotional moments, even giving the two
a minute to compare their swords.

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:30.200
Meanwhile, another brother — Theon — showed
up in the eleventh hour to rescue his sister

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:34.020
Yara, who eventually showed her gratitude
in the most Greyjoy way possible:

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:42.380
Ser Jorah Mormont also got the chance to thank
Sam Tarly, who once cured him of greyscale,

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:46.420
though their reunion took a pretty sour turn
once Daenerys let Sam know what she did to

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:48.120
the rest of his family last season.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:49.340
"Drakaris."

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:56.830
The reunion between Sansa and Tyrion was almost
as tense, since Sansa doesn't believe in him

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:58.040
or his plans anymore.

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:02.580
Another tense reunion took place between Jon
and Sam, especially since a hysterical Sam

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:07.090
holds the key to Jon's parentage and is fresh
off the discovery that he's now the only Tarly

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:07.720
man left.

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:12.500
However, the most fraught was definitely between
Jaime Lannister and Bran Stark once the former

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:16.560
arrives at Winterfell, considering that Jaime
last saw Bran when he pushed him out a window

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:18.660
and tried to kill him in the very first episode.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:23.680
Audiences haven't seen Tormund Giantsbane
— everyone's favorite red-headed wildling

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:27.850
— since he was spotted at Eastwatch last
season as the Wall melted around him, so fans

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:32.230
were likely thrilled to see both Tormund and
Beric Dondarrion alive but not particularly

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:36.030
well at another Northern castle, trying to
figure out how many dead they had to deal

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:38.260
with and whether or not the army was close
by.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:42.720
Ultimately, they find the body of young Ned
Umber, the tiny leader of the House Umber,

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:47.070
pinned to the wall and surrounded by dismembered
limbs in a spiral pattern, which Beric notes

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:48.620
is a "message" from the Night King.

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:53.000
Spiral patterns shouldn't surprise any loyal
Game of Thrones viewers, especially not where

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:57.170
White Walkers are concerned — in the very
first episode, the Walkers arranged the limbs

00:05:57.170 --> 00:06:01.140
of their victims into a circular pattern somewhat
reminiscent of the one that includes poor

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:01.740
dead Ned.

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:06.570
They can also be seen using dead horses to
draw their spiral sign in season 3, when Jon

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:09.060
and the Wildlings go to the Fist of the First
men.

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:11.840
"Always the artists"

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:19.680
So what does the spiral mean?

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:21.110
Well, it's pretty simple.

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:23.780
This is the Night King's way of telling the
armies of Westeros:

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.040
"Hold onto your butts.”

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:28.820
The White Walkers are coming, and probably
in the very next episode.

